<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Encomienda</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The encomienda was a system in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a> by which the crown granted colonists the right to extract labour and tribute from groups of indigenous people, in return for protecting them and instructing them in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. In practice it led to severe abuse, prompting criticism by figures such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bartolome-de-las-casas">Bartolomé de las Casas</a> and attempts at reform through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-laws">New Laws of 1542</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/encomienda.jpg" alt="Encomienda" width="268" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trabajo propio. Reproducción de un dibujo de Felipe Guamán Poma de Ayala. (Own work. Reproduction of a drawing by Fel... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francisco_Hernandez_Giron_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
